y reference value. `no_global_symbol_interposition_between_the_two_libraries` rules this out via `dlsym(RTLD_DEFAULT, …)` plus a behavioural cross-check.\n\n3. **My first run had 3 failures, and all 3 were wrong assumptions in my tests, not translation bugs.** I corrected them against gcc rather than \"fixing\" anything: `INT_MIN % 7` is `-2` (not `-1`); `0` is *not* a fixed point (`step(0) == -3`), so an all-zero array becomes uniformly `-626538949`. The C-vs-Rust comparisons had passed all along.\n\nTwo operational notes: crates.io is blocked here, but `libloading` 0.8.9 was already in the local cargo cache, so builds work with the now-complete `Cargo.lock`. And `c_src/` is untouched apart from the `build/` directory the task instructions require.\n\nRun it all with `./verify.sh` (~4 min) or `./verify.sh --full` (~11 min, includes the four end-to-end runs).","ttft_ms":2294,"ttft_stream_ms":2171,"time_to_request_ms":56,"type":"result","duration_ms":3129883,"uuid":"ab05551a-5f41-4bdc-837e-79fcc3e8ff4c","queued_turn_count":0}
